---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BUSINESS, fullAddress, has } from '../config';

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// OWNER / LEGAL REVIEW RECOMMENDED
// This is an honest, plain-language policy built from how the site actually
// works today (see src/config.ts and the forms). It is NOT legal advice.
//   • Have someone (ideally counsel) review it for your jurisdiction (TN/US).
//   • Providers named below match what is switched on right now:
//       - Forms + email signups → Formspree (config.formspreeEndpoint / newsletterAction)
//       - Hosting + analytics   → Cloudflare Pages + Cloudflare Web Analytics
//       - Maps                  → Google Maps embed (Visit page, click-to-load)
//     If the email list moves to a mailing tool (e.g. Buttondown), name it in
//     "Who we share it with" and link its privacy policy.
//   • Update lastUpdated whenever you change this page.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

const lastUpdated = 'October 9, 2026';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base
  title="Privacy & Cookie Policy | Stone's Throw Coffee"
  description="How Stone's Throw Coffee handles your information: what we collect, how we use it, the limited cookies we use, and how to reach us with privacy questions."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">The fine print, in plain language</p>
      <h1>Privacy &amp; Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        {BUSINESS.name} is built to be a welcoming, low-pressure place, online too. We collect
        as little as possible, we don&rsquo;t sell your information, and we try to explain the rest
        in plain English here.
      </p>
      <p><em>Last updated: {lastUpdated}.</em></p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers this website. {BUSINESS.name} is a coffee shop and community arts space
        {has(fullAddress()) && <>at {fullAddress()}</>}. If you have any questions about it, email us
        at <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}>{BUSINESS.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p><strong>Information you choose to give us.</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Email signups.</strong> If you join our email list, using the sign-up form near the
          bottom of most pages or the sign-up pop-up on our home page, we collect the email address
          you enter so we can send you shop updates. You can ask to be removed at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact &amp; booking forms.</strong> If you message us or pitch an event, art, a
          reading, or a performance, we collect what you put in the form, typically your name,
          email address, and your message, so we can reply.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Information collected automatically.</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Basic server logs.</strong> Like almost every website, our host records standard
          technical information (such as your browser type and a truncated IP address) to keep the
          site secure and working. This is not used to identify you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Privacy-friendly analytics.</strong> We use a cookieless analytics tool
          (Cloudflare Web Analytics) that reports aggregate, anonymous traffic trends. It does not use
          cookies, does not fingerprint you, and does not track you across other sites.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to your message or event request.</li>
        <li>To send you the updates you asked for (and nothing you didn&rsquo;t).</li>
        <li>To keep the website secure, working, and a little better over time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we don&rsquo;t use it for targeted advertising.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We share your information only with the service providers that help us run the site, and only
        as needed for them to do that job:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Forms &amp; email signups.</strong>
          <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Formspree</a>
          receives what you submit through our sign-up, contact, and booking forms, filters out spam,
          and passes it along to our inbox. It may also keep a copy in our account there.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Website hosting &amp; analytics.</strong>
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare</a>
          serves the site and provides the privacy-friendly, aggregate analytics described above.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Maps.</strong> Our Visit page can show a map embedded from Google. See
          <a href="#cookies">Cookies &amp; tracking</a> below.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may also share information if the law requires it. Otherwise, it stays with us.</p>

      <h2 id="cookies">Cookies &amp; tracking</h2>
      <p>
        We keep cookies to a minimum. We don&rsquo;t use advertising cookies, and we don&rsquo;t track
        you across other websites.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Essential only.</strong> The site itself uses only what&rsquo;s necessary to work,
          plus a small piece of browser storage to remember that you&rsquo;ve dismissed our cookie
          notice or our sign-up pop-up (so they don&rsquo;t keep reappearing). Those preferences stay
          on your device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics.</strong> Our analytics are cookieless, so no analytics cookies are set.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The embedded map.</strong> The map on our <a href={`${base}/visit/`}>Visit page</a> is provided
          by Google and can set its own cookies. Because of that, it <strong>does not load until you
          click to load it</strong>. If you&rsquo;d rather not, you can open the location directly in
          Google Maps in a new tab instead. Your choice, every time.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings at any time; the site will still
        work.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Unsubscribe</strong> from our emails any time by emailing us at
          <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}> {BUSINESS.email}</a>, or by using the unsubscribe link
          in any email we send.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Access, correct, or delete</strong> the information you&rsquo;ve given us by emailing
          <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}> {BUSINESS.email}</a>. We&rsquo;ll take care of it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your information only as long as we need it for the purpose you gave it to us, for
        example, until you unsubscribe, or for a reasonable time after we&rsquo;ve answered your
        message, and then we delete or anonymize it.
      </p>

      <h2>Children&rsquo;s privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our website isn&rsquo;t directed at children under 13, and we don&rsquo;t knowingly collect
        their information. Everyone&rsquo;s welcome in the shop, but the forms here are meant for adults.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        We link out to places like our GoFundMe and our social pages. Those sites have their own
        privacy practices, and this policy doesn&rsquo;t cover them.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how we handle your information, we&rsquo;ll update this page and the &ldquo;last
        updated&rdquo; date above.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about your privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}>{BUSINESS.email}</a>
        {has(fullAddress()) && <> or write to us at {fullAddress()}</>}. A real human will read it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
